# Repo had no .gitignore until 2026-08-14. Added when the LoRA lane's ~98 MB of
# working data turned out to be entirely untracked: the rule below is what makes
# committing the lane safe rather than a 100 MB blob push.
#
# Principle: track the PROVENANCE, not the BYTES. Anything that is (a) large and
# (b) either deterministically regenerable from tracked code or already published
# as a Kaggle dataset is excluded here — and in every such case a small manifest
# carrying shapes, counts and sha256s IS tracked, so the artifact can be rebuilt
# and verified without living in git history.

# LoRA probe adapters: 2 x 41,962,184 B, built by duck_eval/lora/make_probe_adapters.py.
# Published as canivel/arc3-lora-probe-adapters (2026-08-14). Provenance is kept in
# runs/lora_lane/probe_adapters/PROBE_ADAPTERS.json (tensor counts, param counts,
# sha256_16, nonzero_lora_B_modules) — that file is TRACKED on purpose.
runs/lora_lane/probe_adapters/**/*.safetensors

# Kernel-output site-packages dumps: third-party wheels (.so/.py) pulled back inside
# a kernel's output for diagnosis. The DIAGNOSIS lives in the .log files next to them,
# which are tracked; the wheels themselves are 16 MB of somebody else's binaries.
runs/kernel_pulls/**/vllm-site-packages/

# Model weight snapshots and checkpoints — always served from Kaggle datasets.
_weights/
_pretrained_ds/

__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
